      "side": 1,
      "message": "Note that dashes and commas are converted to underscores by DT_NODE_FULL_NAME. So this should be checking `psl_in` not `psl-in`.\n\nHowever, I don\u0027t like using the node name to figure out the wake source mapping.\n\nThe PSL pin nodes already provide the `psl-offset` parameter, which is what I think you\u0027re trying to derive.\n\n```\n/* node \u0027/pinctrl/periph-psl-in1\u0027 defined in main/dts/arm/nuvoton/npcx/npcx9/npcx9-pinctrl.dtsi:395 */\npsl_in1_gpd2: periph-psl-in1 {\n    pinmux \u003d \u003c \u0026altd_npsl_in1_sl \u003e;       /* in main/dts/arm/nuvoton/npcx/npcx9/npcx9-pinctrl.dtsi:396 */\n    psl-offset \u003d \u003c 0x0 \u003e;                 /* in main/dts/arm/nuvoton/npcx/npcx9/npcx9-pinctrl.dtsi:397 */\n    psl-polarity \u003d \u003c \u0026altd_psl_in1_ahi \u003e; /* in main/dts/arm/nuvoton/npcx/npcx9/npcx9-pinctrl.dtsi:398 */\n    psl-in-mode \u003d \"edge\";                 /* in ../../platform/ec/zephyr/program/bluey/psl.dtsi:16 */\n    psl-in-pol \u003d \"high-rising\";           /* in ../../platform/ec/zephyr/program/bluey/psl.dtsi:17 */\n    phandle \u003d \u003c 0x13d \u003e;                  /* in ../../platform/ec/zephyr/program/bluey/psl.dtsi:36 */\n};\n```\n\n`DT_FOREACH_PROP_ELEM` below iterates through the phandles assigned to `pinctrl-0`.\n\nYou can use `DT_PROP(node_id, psl_offset)` to get the bit number.",
